+# Fresh B09-accepted interface assessment
+
+Exact accepted baseline `1e6b11a47370f1c7c4659a32443fc1afda597bac`; all72 reads and six write inputs verified at their contract identities. WP39 (325 lines) and WP40 (314 lines) were read in full at this baseline, including shared003 qualifiers and selection/registration/execution distinctions. WP38§§5–6 and WP42§§6–7 were additionally read at the accepted identities. Source reads are text only at reference `8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b`; no game behavior was executed. Original findings, complete current qualifications/effective constraints, root/extension precedence and fixed acceptance projections were reread. Global extension source re-review is not claimed.
+
+| B14 reader boundary | Newly accepted condition and consequence for authoring |
+| --- | --- |
+| WP59§§1–4/8/10/11; WT01/03/04/07 | WP39§7.3 samples world inputs at creation. Explicit battle rule overrides weather/terrain/environment; world category otherwise maps Rain/Storm→Rain, Hail→Hail, Sandstorm→Sandstorm, Sun→Sun. Only configured Storm/Fog set default battle terrain. Fishing encounters sample facing terrain; others sample feet, with Forest+grass→ForestGrass. Map cave environment forces time2, otherwise TIME_SHADING gates live-hour time. Local 24-hour/weather data must not replace rule precedence or imply live resampling throughout battle. Connected edge duration20 corrects only world display sequencing, preserving accepted WP11/WP16 fixed fades. |
+| WP59§§5–7; WT14–25 and engine field item rows | Public wild wrapper constructs once before optional single-target override; direct core skip/start precedes construction. Raw result2/5 versus other result normalization and override bypass remain separate. Field capability eligibility, confirmation and actual effect are three behavioral phases; registration/source tables are not future architecture. Local DIVE ascent and WATERFALL true-without-start do not establish successful encounter/battle. Preserve needed literal move IDs, markers, returns, callback failures and ordered state writes under shared003. |
+| Fishing§§1/3/5/7–9/12–13; FS01–15 and missing valid-start row | fishing_battles increments on fishing success before encounter request; candidate creation failure and no/empty table remain distinct. WP36 type lifetime on first/second empty candidate does not become a battle result. Normal public call return is not victory: raw2/5 normalize false, other results true, overrides may bypass normalization. Valid start event bypasses built-in movement/lock/animation but does not bypass final cleanup. Capture and actual battle environment retain accepted WP38/WP39 conditions; no new blanket partner restoration premise. |
+| Berry whole bidirectional reader, especially§§2–3/5–6/12; BP rows | Shared003 separates per-plot domain state and frozen mechanism choice from event-variable/container organization. UI current configuration remains distinct from object mechanism; stored mulch parameters are applied before the old/new settlement split. Inspection of accepted B09 shared controls found no local battle consumer that changes the mulch/watering/sparkle gates; this is bounded author analysis, not an independent NOT_AFFECTED receipt or absence-of-plan-edge proof. The complete four-way B09/B14 stale-reader relationship remains gated. |
+| WP61§§1–5; FP01/02/06/08/09/24 | Actual completion notification precedes player post-step; forcing/interpreter branch can emit another general notification under full uninterrupted movement premises. It returns before global/player/transfer/encounter chain. No inference that this fixture triggers battle or that all blocked/automatic/ended routes have two notifications. Ordinary route separately carries handled state; its poison row needs explicit POISON_IN_FIELD=true, step multiple4, handled false, able snapshot and member-state gates. |
+| WP61§6.2–6.3; FP12/14/27/30 | Daily gate can be satisfied by an infected egg, while inner decrement affects only infected non-eggs; empty eligible set still permits timestamp write. Battle-end propagation is separate: after capture receipt, fix current-player infection sources and only neighbor stage0 targets; new infections do not chain and cured members do not qualify. Daily correction cannot silently redefine accepted WP42 propagation. |
+| WP61§§7–8/12–13; FP17–24/26–28/31 | Defeat/draw with canLose and no-canLose separate; restore BGM/BGS before blackout in the ordinary no-canLose world handoff. Core after-battle partner existence healing differs from actual participating partner's separate ordered battle members. Healing does not reset held items. Preserve normal-return, capture/storage healing and missing-home early-return qualifications; local escape producer/presentation correction does not alter existing blackout branches or imply real event reachability. |
+| WP61 post-battle current-item consumers and shared003 | Accepted B09-G-O01 is one terminal restoration traversal. Default six-player full party A..F, actual participating partner, shared creature identities in separate ordered battle members, X/Y inert distinct items on A/B and others/catch empty, double-wild first defeated then other caught, receive0 joins caught creature and boxesA, valid storage/callbacks and no other mutations: boxedA=Y, liveB=empty. There is no later shifted-current-player restoration traversal restoring B. World pickup/honey/evolution consume actual resulting held items; do not claim every initial item is restored correctly or collapse shared identity into a mandatory source array. |
+| WP40/full command readers, shared003 and both catalogs | Accepted NearAlly fixture has live user0, near2 fainted/no reserve, far4 live, normal command entry. Initial selection and USE register4; nil text differs from eligible empty text and button selection differs from member highlight. Unchanged layout/life plus normal target resolution rejects far4 without eligible near fallback; no assertion of final effect/PP/message. The both-nonself-allies-fainted/self0 B033 residual remains independently owned. This prevents “selected/registered therefore effective” wording in field/item interfaces; no new B14 behavioral finding or catalog expansion beyond assigned rows. |
+
+Both whole catalogs remain exclusive-write interfaces. The contract requires independently supported exact affected dispositions for B02/B03/B04/B06/B07/B08/B09. Proposed changes touch shared bytes/data/caller conditions, so request separate bounded candidate and actual affected review as applicable; do not transfer an old PASS or manufacture a lease/chronology certificate. No independent review has yet occurred. B10 output is not an upstream approval, was not consumed, and its WP46 reverse reader remains a future B10 gate.
+
+Every sensitivity class in the old preflight reread inventory is addressed above at the accepted successor, including original counterparts, management/report corrections, indirect capture/end consumers and the complete catalogs. The fresh full72/6 refreeze protects paths beyond this bounded semantic assessment. Final authoring, full24 contribution coverage and candidate review are still pending at the original-scope checkpoint; this record does not approve them.
